forumulate:index/connector:Connector.description:
A chat or AI product connected to one space (Intercom, Zendesk, a custom provider...): installed with its <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`config`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Config`" pulumi-lang-go="`config`" pulumi-lang-python="`config`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`config`" pulumi-lang-java="`config`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`config`">`config`</span>, optionally embedded on the reader and/or given read access to the space's knowledge base. `GET /orgs/{orgId}/connector-providers` lists the providers and the config fields each needs. For the organization-level e-signature, meeting and wallet connectors see <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`forumulate.ServiceConnector`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`forumulate.ServiceConnector`" pulumi-lang-go="`ServiceConnector`" pulumi-lang-python="`ServiceConnector`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`forumulate.ServiceConnector`" pulumi-lang-java="`forumulate.ServiceConnector`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`forumulate_service_connector`">`forumulate.ServiceConnector`</span>.

<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`config`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Config`" pulumi-lang-go="`config`" pulumi-lang-python="`config`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`config`" pulumi-lang-java="`config`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`config`">`config`</span> is sensitive and write-only: the API reports only which fields are set (<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`configuredFields`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ConfiguredFields`" pulumi-lang-go="`configuredFields`" pulumi-lang-python="`configured_fields`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`configuredFields`" pulumi-lang-java="`configuredFields`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`configured_fields`">`configuredFields`</span>) and which are still missing (<span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`missingFields`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`MissingFields`" pulumi-lang-go="`missingFields`" pulumi-lang-python="`missing_fields`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`missingFields`" pulumi-lang-java="`missingFields`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`missing_fields`">`missingFields`</span>), so a changed secret cannot be detected. With <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`mintToken " pulumi-lang-dotnet="`MintToken " pulumi-lang-go="`mintToken " pulumi-lang-python="`mint_token " pulumi-lang-yaml="`mintToken " pulumi-lang-java="`mintToken " pulumi-lang-hcl="`mint_token ">`mintToken </span>= true` the connector gets an access token for the product to read the knowledge base with; it is shown once and kept, sensitive, in <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`token`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Token`" pulumi-lang-go="`token`" pulumi-lang-python="`token`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`token`" pulumi-lang-java="`token`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`token`">`token`</span>. Change <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`tokenRotation`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`TokenRotation`" pulumi-lang-go="`tokenRotation`" pulumi-lang-python="`token_rotation`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`tokenRotation`" pulumi-lang-java="`tokenRotation`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`token_rotation`">`tokenRotation`</span> to mint a new one.

## Example Usage

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as forumulate from "@forumulate/pulumi";

const config = new pulumi.Config();
const intercomToken = config.require("intercomToken");
// Connect a chat product to a docs space: embed its widget on the reader and
// let it read the space's knowledge base.
const intercom = new forumulate.Connector("intercom", {
    spaceId: docs.id,
    providerId: "intercom",
    config: {
        workspaceId: "abc123",
        accessToken: intercomToken,
    },
    embedEnabled: true,
    knowledgeEnabled: true,
    knowledgeScopes: [
        "search",
        "ask",
        "llms",
    ],
    appearance: {
        primaryColor: "#0b835b",
        colorScheme: "system",
        position: "right",
        greeting: "Questions? Ask us.",
    },
    mintToken: true,
});
export const intercomKnowledgeToken = intercom.token;
export const intercomMissingFields = intercom.missingFields;
