forumulate:index/site:Site.description:
A site gathers public spaces under one address so they share a header, a footer and a theme. <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`spaceIds`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`SpaceIds`" pulumi-lang-go="`spaceIds`" pulumi-lang-python="`space_ids`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`spaceIds`" pulumi-lang-java="`spaceIds`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`space_ids`">`spaceIds`</span> is its membership, <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`configJson`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ConfigJson`" pulumi-lang-go="`configJson`" pulumi-lang-python="`config_json`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`configJson`" pulumi-lang-java="`configJson`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`config_json`">`configJson`</span> its shared chrome and look (header and footer links, theme, search, SEO, analytics, ...), and <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`pageMounts`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`PageMounts`" pulumi-lang-go="`pageMounts`" pulumi-lang-python="`page_mounts`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`pageMounts`" pulumi-lang-java="`pageMounts`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`page_mounts`">`pageMounts`</span> publishes single pages of member spaces at a path of the site (`/pricing`) or at its root.

Destroying a site dissolves the grouping; every space in it survives with its own content and theme.

