forumulate:index/siteManifest:SiteManife.description:
A whole site as one document: the `version: 2` manifest of `PUT /orgs/{orgId}/manifest`, the same one `forumulate plan` and `forumulate apply` use. Spaces with their SEO, theme, locales and layout, collections, pages from Markdown, forum categories, sites, domains, webhooks, status monitors, connectors, interface strings and organization settings can all be declared in it.

`pulumi preview` runs the API's own dry run and prints the manifest plan's steps (create, update, delete, field by field) as warnings, and a manifest the API would refuse fails the plan on <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`manifestJson`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ManifestJson`" pulumi-lang-go="`manifestJson`" pulumi-lang-python="`manifest_json`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`manifestJson`" pulumi-lang-java="`manifestJson`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`manifest_json`">`manifestJson`</span>. `pulumi up` applies it; the apply is idempotent, additive (nothing undeclared is deleted unless <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`prune`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Prune`" pulumi-lang-go="`prune`" pulumi-lang-python="`prune`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`prune`" pulumi-lang-java="`prune`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`prune`">`prune`</span>) and stops at the first failing unit, which is kept. A page or setting changed outside Terraform shows as pending changes at the next refresh and is put back by the next apply.

Compose the document with Terraform values: <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`manifestJson " pulumi-lang-dotnet="`ManifestJson " pulumi-lang-go="`manifestJson " pulumi-lang-python="`manifest_json " pulumi-lang-yaml="`manifestJson " pulumi-lang-java="`manifestJson " pulumi-lang-hcl="`manifest_json ">`manifestJson </span>= jsonencode({ version = 2, spaces = [...] })`, or `jsonencode(yamldecode(file("forumulate.yaml")))`. Destroying the resource forgets the manifest; set <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`destroyPrunes`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`DestroyPrunes`" pulumi-lang-go="`destroyPrunes`" pulumi-lang-python="`destroy_prunes`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`destroyPrunes`" pulumi-lang-java="`destroyPrunes`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`destroy_prunes`">`destroyPrunes`</span> to delete what it created (see below).

## Example Usage

<!--Start PulumiCodeChooser -->
```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import * as forumulate from "@forumulate/pulumi";
import * as std from "@pulumi/std";

// The whole site as one document, planned and applied through the API's own
// manifest dry run. `pulumi preview` prints every step the manifest would take.
const site = new forumulate.SiteManifest("site", {
    manifestJson: JSON.stringify({
        version: 2,
        spaces: [
            {
                slug: "docs",
                name: "Docs",
                type: "DOCS",
                visibility: "PUBLIC",
                locales: [{
                    code: "es",
                    label: "Español",
                }],
                seo: {
                    seoTitle: "Acme documentation",
                },
                redirects: [{
                    from: "/start",
                    to: "/docs/getting-started",
                }],
            },
            {
                slug: "blog",
                name: "Blog",
                type: "BLOG",
                visibility: "PUBLIC",
            },
        ],
        pages: [{
            space: "docs",
            slug: "getting-started",
            title: "Getting started",
            body: "Welcome to **Acme**.",
        }],
        sites: [{
            slug: "main",
            name: "Acme",
            spaces: [
                "docs",
                "blog",
            ],
        }],
        orgSettings: {
            "search.typo_tolerance": true,
        },
    }),
    prune: true,
});
// Or keep the document in YAML beside your Markdown:
//   manifest_json = jsonencode(yamldecode(file("${path.module}/forumulate.yaml")))
export const docsSpaceId = site.ids["spaces/docs"];
export const manualSteps = std.jsondecodeOutput({
    input: site.manualJson,
}).result;
