forumulate:index/space:Space.description:
A space: one docs site, forum, blog, changelog, status page and so on. The <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`type`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Type`" pulumi-lang-go="`type`" pulumi-lang-python="`type`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`type`" pulumi-lang-java="`type`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`type`">`type`</span> decides its tabs, its piece names, its layouts and which other resources apply to it (see the <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`forumulate.getSpaceTypes`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`forumulate.getSpaceTypes`" pulumi-lang-go="`getSpaceTypes`" pulumi-lang-python="`get_space_types`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`forumulate.getSpaceTypes`" pulumi-lang-java="`forumulate.getSpaceTypes`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`data.forumulate_space_types`">`forumulate.getSpaceTypes`</span> data source). Creating a space and then managing its theme, SEO, redirects and settings is <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`forumulate.Space`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`forumulate.Space`" pulumi-lang-go="`Space`" pulumi-lang-python="`Space`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`forumulate.Space`" pulumi-lang-java="`forumulate.Space`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`forumulate_space`">`forumulate.Space`</span> plus <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`forumulate.SpaceSettings`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`forumulate.SpaceSettings`" pulumi-lang-go="`SpaceSettings`" pulumi-lang-python="`SpaceSettings`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`forumulate.SpaceSettings`" pulumi-lang-java="`forumulate.SpaceSettings`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`forumulate_space_settings`">`forumulate.SpaceSettings`</span>.

Destroying a space moves it to the trash (readers and the API stop seeing it; the platform can restore it). Set <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`destroyOnDelete " pulumi-lang-dotnet="`DestroyOnDelete " pulumi-lang-go="`destroyOnDelete " pulumi-lang-python="`destroy_on_delete " pulumi-lang-yaml="`destroyOnDelete " pulumi-lang-java="`destroyOnDelete " pulumi-lang-hcl="`destroy_on_delete ">`destroyOnDelete </span>= true` to make it permanent and free the slug.

