forumulate:index/spaceLocale:SpaceLocale.description:
A language a docs space publishes in. Adding one gives every page a translatable twin at a locale-prefixed address (`/docs/es/...`) and is the prerequisite for hand-written and machine translations. The code <span pulumi-lang-nodejs="`default`" pulumi-lang-dotnet="`Default`" pulumi-lang-go="`default`" pulumi-lang-python="`default`" pulumi-lang-yaml="`default`" pulumi-lang-java="`default`" pulumi-lang-hcl="`default`">`default`</span> relabels the source language (shown as "Original" until you name it); it exists already, so it is only renamed, and destroying it changes nothing.

